{
  "requirement": "Habeas's bundled agent instructions MUST direct agents to run Cargo doctests\nseparately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation:** `requirements.test-coverage.guidance.doctests` has one MUST. Habeas's bundled agent instructions must direct agents to run Cargo doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`. The requirement declaration anchors it with `:impl:` to `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md`, `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md`, `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` and `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`.\n\n**Test:** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_default_to_process_coverage_and_keep_artifacts_disposable]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n- In a loop over all three bundled skills (`habeas`, `habeas-evidence`, `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`), it asserts that the whitespace-collapsed skill text contains `` `cargo test --doc --workspace` ``. The failure message names the skill, so a missing command in any one skill fails the test.\n- For `habeas`, `assert_text` requires the directive sentence \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\". This covers both the command and the \"separately\" wording.\n- For `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, `assert_text` requires \"run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\" inside the \"Follow the habeas skill's ...\" sentence.\n- It also asserts the same directive in `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`, which is an anchored implementation site.\n\n**Other skills:** I searched `habeas-refactor` and `habeas-requirements` for test-run guidance (`cargo test`, `cargo nextest`, `habeas coverage` and similar) and found none. They give no test-run instructions, so they have no doctest direction to verify.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no obligation without a test and no assertion that fails to enforce the text. The exact-sentence assertions would fail if the directive were removed or reworded, for example if it dropped \"separately\" or changed the command.",
